- What strategies would you use to measure and reduce test flakiness in CI?

## Why This Is Asked
Advanced production systems require testing for exactly-once semantics under high throughput, event-time processing with late data, and schema evolution. This question probes test strategy, data generation, and resilience to restarts and migrations.

## Key Concepts
- Exactly-once semantics in stream processing (Kafka Streams, Flink)
- Event-time processing and late data handling with watermarks
- Schema evolution and compatibility via schema registry
- Replayable test data and deterministic outputs
- Canary releases and CI/CD integration for fast feedback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple deterministic test harness sketch
function runTest(events, process, compare) {
  const outputs = process(events);
  // restart simulation
  const outputs2 = process(events);
  if (JSON.stringify(outputs) !== JSON.stringify(outputs2)) {
    throw new Error("Non-deterministic outputs across restarts");
  }
  // validate idempotent
  const dupEvents = events.concat(events);
  const outputsDup = process(dupEvents);
  if (JSON.stringify(outputsDup) !== JSON.stringify(outputs)) {
    throw new Error("Non-idempotent processing on duplicates");
  }
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test state snapshot recovery for a rolling upgrade without downtime?
- How would you measure impact on latency under bursty traffic and constrain drift during schema upgrades?

